From b47e8f9e01e14014c05ed4546663dde9610b0001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:54:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] 3D viewer: render the OpenGL view in stereo

Add a setting to ask for a stereo (quad-buffer) visual and to set the
eye separation.  When the canvas got a stereo visual, the OpenGL
engine is rendered once for each eye, the left eye into GL_BACK_LEFT
and the right eye into GL_BACK_RIGHT, from the same scene data.  The
pivot markers follow the eye camera; the navigator gizmo, a 2D
overlay, is drawn identically in both eyes.

The setting is read when the viewer is opened.  The raytracing engine
and the screenshot canvas stay mono, and a display without stereo
visuals gets the mono visual as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
